      "location": "2.1",
      "defect": "missing-hypothesis",
      "evidence": "Step 2.1 says that when a block lies in K one can “rewrite it as the canonical element of K and push it across.” Decidable membership supplies only a yes/no test. The cited normal-form theorem supplies normal forms relative to fixed transversals, chosen non-effectively, and does not provide an algorithm translating a discovered element of K in G to its corresponding word in H. Such effective embedding/translation data is necessary for the advertised algorithm.",
