      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "The cited normal-closure result explicitly says that for n=0 the displayed product is the identity. For P=<x | emptyset> and the empty word w, w is null and has area 0, but there is no positive-length relator expression because R is empty. Thus the assertion that the defining set contains “at least one positive integer m” is false.",
