      "evidence": "Steps 1.1–2.1 show only that one semidecision procedure may fail to halt on negative inputs. That does not show that no different decision algorithm exists: a recursive language can also have a halting-only semidecider. A refutation needs an unsolvable-word-problem recursive presentation, such as the Novikov-Boone example; none is invoked here.",
