      "evidence": "Take the triangle graph with all groups trivial, T={a,b}, and T'={b,c}. In pi_1(G,T), c is the sole non-tree generator. The prescribed map sends c to p_T'(o)c p_T'(t)^(-1), but all T' path terms and c are trivial in pi_1(G,T'), since c is a T' edge. Hence c maps to 1, so the claimed composites cannot fix every non-tree generator as step 3.1 asserts.",
