      "defect": "ill-formed",
      "evidence": "The definition independently chooses a lift for every oriented quotient edge, but does not require the reverse choices to satisfy tilde(bar e)=bar(tilde e). It then sets G_e=Stab(tilde e). The graph-of-groups definition requires G_e=G_(bar e) for a geometric edge; independently chosen reverse lifts generally have conjugate, not equal, stabilizers. Therefore the prescribed data need not form a graph of groups.",
